From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Sun, 10 Jul 2022 21:37:07 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] scripts/conmakehash: don't embed the build path in output

Kbuild invokes this as "scripts/conmakehash $(src)/$(FONTMAPFILE)"; for
out-of-tree (O=) builds $(src) is $(srctree)/drivers/tty/vt, so argv[1]
is an absolute path containing ${WORKDIR}/${TMPDIR}. That path ends up
in the "automatically generated by" comment of consolemap_deftbl.c and
trips the "buildpaths" QA check on the -src package.

Strip the $srctree prefix (exported by the top-level Makefile) from the
input filename before printing it, the same fix as upstream commit
2fca0fd71981 ("vt/conmakehash: improve reproducibility"), which instead
added a second argument for the capture name and updated the Makefile
to pass it. This kernel predates both that move to drivers/tty/vt/ and
the abs_srctree export, so adapt the fix to scripts/conmakehash.c and
to the srctree variable this Makefile actually exports.

[Herman: adapted for pre-abs_srctree kernel]

Originally by Bruce Ashfield <bruce.ashfield@gmail.com>, taken from shr-distribution/linux tissot/4.9/halium-9.0 (2291ed623f81), where tissot builds with it.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Backport
---
 scripts/conmakehash.c | 16 +++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/scripts/conmakehash.c b/scripts/conmakehash.c
index 61bbda54cf1..02fb45c4c01 100644
--- a/scripts/conmakehash.c
+++ b/scripts/conmakehash.c
@@ -80,6 +80,7 @@ int main(int argc, char *argv[])
 {
   FILE *ctbl;
   char *tblname;
+  char *rel_tblname;
   char buffer[65536];
   int fontlen;
   int i, nuni, nent;
@@ -104,6 +105,19 @@ int main(int argc, char *argv[])
 	}
     }
 
+  /* Strip $srctree from the input path so the generated file doesn't
+     embed the build path (Kbuild exports srctree as an absolute path
+     for O= builds). */
+  rel_tblname = tblname;
+  {
+    char *srctree = getenv("srctree");
+    size_t srctree_len = srctree ? strlen(srctree) : 0;
+
+    if (srctree_len && !strncmp(tblname, srctree, srctree_len) &&
+	tblname[srctree_len] == '/')
+      rel_tblname = tblname + srctree_len + 1;
+  }
+
   /* For now we assume the default font is always 256 characters. */
   fontlen = 256;
 
@@ -256,7 +270,7 @@ int main(int argc, char *argv[])
 #include <linux/types.h>\n\
 \n\
 u8 dfont_unicount[%d] = \n\
-{\n\t", argv[1], fontlen);
+{\n\t", rel_tblname, fontlen);
 
   for ( i = 0 ; i < fontlen ; i++ )
     {
